{"Come to the Gray’s-Inn Coffee-House, Pinto said, “and I will tell you how the notch came to the ax.” And we walked down Holborn at about \003thirty-seven minutes past six o’clock\004.","The Notch on the Ax","William Makepeace Thackeray",true},
},
["18:38"]={
{"He took the same route every day, spoke to the same security guard for the same amount of time, took the same lift to the same floor, hung his same coat in the same place and sat at the same desk until lunchtime, when he brought the same sandwich (ham and pickle on brown) from the same sandwich shop. At half past five every day he did the whole journey in reverse, reaching home at between 18:24 on a good day and \00318:38\004 on a bad one.","The Case of the Wayward Professor","Gareth P. Jones",true},
},
["18:39"]={
{"At \003twenty-one minutes to seven\004, Yuri will sit down at your table, or maybe at the one next to it. That will obviously depend on how busy the cafe is.","Manhunt","James Barrington",true},
},
["18:40"]={
{"It was \003six-forty\004 on the same Tuesday before George Chandler-Powell had finished his list of private patients at St. Angela’s Hospital. Pulling off his operating gown, he felt paradoxically both exhausted and restless.","The Private Patient","P.D. James",true},
{"Having to change ’buses, I allowed plenty of time — in fact, too much; for we arrived at \003twenty minutes to seven\004, and Franching, so the servant said, had only just gone up to dress.","The Diary of a Nobody","George and Weedon Grossmith",true},
},
["18:41"]={
{"He made it to Grand Central well in advance. Stillman’s train was not due to arrive until \003six forty-one\004, but Quinn wanted time to study the geography of the place, to make sure that Stillman would not be able to slip away from him.","The New York Trilogy","Paul Auster",true},
},
["18:42"]={
{"It was \003six forty-two\004. Unless Emma was spending the weekend out of town she would probably be at home.","A Taste for Death","P.D. James",true},
},
["18:43"]={
{"Bev was no clock-watcher, but by \00318:43\004 she’d had enough. A stack of papers at her left elbow represented eliminations: calls put in, checks made, follow-ups done and dusted. At the right lay further actions.","Bad Press","Maureen Carter",true},
},
["18:45"]={
{"The black boy’s dwarf head swivels and comes nose to knuckle with that hand. He frowns at it, then takes a quick check where’s the other two black boys just in case, and tells McMurphy they don’t open the cabinet till \003six-forty-five\004. “It’s a policy,” he says.","One Flew Over the Cuckoo’s Nest","Ken Kesey",false},
{"Let me see now. You had a drink at the Continental at six ten.\n“Yes.”\n“And at \003six forty-five\004 you were talking to another journalist at the door of the Majestic?”\n“Yes, Wilkins. I told you all this, Vigot, before. That night.”","The Quiet American","Graham Greene",true},
{"\003Six forty-five\004, called Louie. “Did you hear, Ming,” he asked, “did you hear?”\n“Yes, Taddy, I heard.”\n“What is it?” asked Tommy. “The new baby, listen, the new baby.”","The Man Who Loved Children","Christina Stead",true},
{"It was a \003quarter to seven\004 when I let myself into the office and clicked the light on and picked a piece of paper off the floor. It was a notice from the Green Feather Messenger Service …","The High Window","Raymond Chandler",true},
